WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.867 --> 00:00:02.102
- Before we started the show,

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:03.737
I was talking about the
five Gs with my guys.

00:00:03.737 --> 00:00:05.538
Can we go through the five Gs?

00:00:05.538 --> 00:00:07.707
- Of course I love the five Gs.

00:00:07.707 --> 00:00:08.575
- I know, I know.

00:00:08.575 --> 00:00:09.976
Take it away.

00:00:09.976 --> 00:00:13.713
("Rubin Report" intro music)

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:19.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm Dave Rubin, and
joining me today is author

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:21.921 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the world-famous book,
"Rich Dad, Poor Dad"

00:00:21.921 --> 00:00:25.492
and author of the brand new
book, "Capitalist Manifesto:

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:28.728
"How Entrepreneurs
Can Save Capitalism".

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.797
Robert Kiyosaki welcome
to "The Ruben Report".

00:00:30.797 --> 00:00:32.665 align:start size:94% position:6%
- Well, thank you, honored
to be on your program.

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:34.701 align:start size:84% position:16%
You're doing a great
job. Thank you.

00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:35.902
- Oh, I appreciate that.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:37.971
Well, I am glad to have you on

00:00:37.971 --> 00:00:42.942 align:start size:97% position:3%
because in my last book I
did one chapter on capitalism

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:45.045
to try to save capitalism,

00:00:45.045 --> 00:00:47.013 align:start size:84% position:16%
but your whole
life has been about

00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:49.015
trying to save capitalism.

00:00:49.015 --> 00:00:51.851
So before we get into
capitalism itself,

00:00:51.851 --> 00:00:54.054
give me a little bit of
your bio for the people

00:00:54.054 --> 00:00:55.955
that maybe have not read it

00:00:55.955 --> 00:00:57.390
because it's quite extraordinary

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.159
and pretty much explains exactly

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:01.494 align:start size:97% position:3%
why you care about the
things that you write about.

00:01:01.494 --> 00:01:03.596 align:start size:88% position:13%
- Right. It's more
than capitalism, David,

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:05.065
I'm fighting for our freedom.

00:01:06.232 --> 00:01:09.002 align:start size:81% position:19%
And there's a fine
line, you know,

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.171
between that and capitalism.

00:01:11.171 --> 00:01:12.372
But my background is,

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:15.275
I'm fourth-generation
Japanese-American.

00:01:15.275 --> 00:01:17.410
And the reason I say that is,

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:20.547
during the Vietnam War
I was a U.S. Marine,

00:01:20.547 --> 00:01:21.848
and some people think,

00:01:21.848 --> 00:01:24.250 align:start size:88% position:13%
"You fought for the
Japanese Marine Corps?"

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:26.486
(both laughing)

00:01:26.486 --> 00:01:28.388
I always thought that was funny.

00:01:28.388 --> 00:01:32.826
And then I've been accused
of being a white supremacist

00:01:32.826 --> 00:01:36.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I support freedom,
I support capitalism.

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:37.931
I said, "I looked
in the mirror,"

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:41.468
I said, "well, I'm still
not white." (chuckles)

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:43.369
It's just,

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:49.742
it's amazing how
little people know,

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:50.910
it shocks me.

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.412
So anyway, my background is

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:54.080
I'm fourth-generation
Japanese-American,

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:57.083
I was raised in Hawaii
and I had the misfortune

00:01:57.083 --> 00:02:00.620
or good fortune to go
to a rich kid school,

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:02.589
a rich white kid school

00:02:02.589 --> 00:02:05.592 align:start size:84% position:16%
in a little town
called Hilo, Hawaii.

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:07.861
So on one side of
the street, I mean,

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:12.098
exactly opposite was
Hilo Union School,

00:02:12.098 --> 00:02:14.634
and Hilo Union School was
for all the minorities,

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.569 align:start size:84% position:16%
the Japanese, the
Chinese, the Filipino,

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:18.438
the Portuguese and all this.

00:02:18.438 --> 00:02:20.673
And directly across the street

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:24.010
was Riverside School
for the rich kids.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:27.247
And I just, my father was
head of education poor dad,

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.049
and he didn't gyrate,
manipulate anything,

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:31.751 align:start size:84% position:16%
I just happened to
fall into the district

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.052
with the rich kids school.

00:02:34.187 --> 00:02:35.622
I was nine years old, I'm going,

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:38.625 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Well, how come some
people are rich,

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:41.261
"and why are some people poor?"

00:02:41.261 --> 00:02:42.462
And as you know, David,

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.897 align:start size:84% position:16%
one of the biggest
problems we have today

00:02:43.897 --> 00:02:46.065 align:start size:84% position:16%
is this gap between
rich and poor.

00:02:46.065 --> 00:02:48.301
It sets up revolution,

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.870
and I don't think
that's a mistake.

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.273 align:start size:81% position:19%
So I go to this
rich kid's school,

00:02:53.273 --> 00:02:56.643
and I asked the teachers,
"Well, how do I get rich?"

00:02:56.643 --> 00:02:59.045 align:start size:84% position:16%
Well, she said, "You
stay in school."

00:02:59.045 --> 00:03:00.813 align:start size:84% position:16%
I said, "My poor dad
stayed in school,

00:03:00.813 --> 00:03:03.583
he's still poor." (laughs)

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:05.151
You know how kids are, they go,

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:06.152
"(speaking in foreign language),

00:03:06.152 --> 00:03:07.654 align:start size:88% position:13%
"what's happening here?"
- Yeah.

00:03:07.654 --> 00:03:11.391
- So that's how the story of
"Rich Dad, Poor Dad" started.

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:13.026
But the real test
of the thing was

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:16.863 align:start size:84% position:16%
that was that movie,
"Caddyshack", you
know, years ago,

00:03:16.863 --> 00:03:18.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
Chevy Chase and all those
characters. (laughs)

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:21.401 align:start size:84% position:16%
- I've seen it
roughly 4,000 times.

00:03:21.401 --> 00:03:23.703 align:start size:97% position:3%
- But that's the classic story
of rich and poor, you know.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:28.708
So by 10, I take up the game
of golf and I have to hitchhike

00:03:29.442 --> 00:03:30.777
to the country club,

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:32.579
but I have to sit
in the caddy shack

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:37.083
and my classmates are
in the country club.

00:03:37.083 --> 00:03:38.952 align:start size:88% position:13%
And I keep asking
myself again, you know,

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:40.453
(speaking in foreign language),

00:03:40.453 --> 00:03:45.091 align:start size:97% position:3%
how come some people are rich
and some people are poor?

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:47.360 align:start size:84% position:16%
And it kind of became
my lifelong quest

00:03:48.228 --> 00:03:49.295
and question on that.

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:50.997
I did go to military school.

00:03:50.997 --> 00:03:53.132
I mean, I was a
horrible student,

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:56.369 align:start size:97% position:3%
but I got congressional
nominations, the Naval Academy

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:58.504
and U.S. Merch Marine
Academy in New York.

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:00.039
I took Merch Marine Academy.

00:04:00.907 --> 00:04:03.443
And in 1965, when I went there,

00:04:03.443 --> 00:04:06.246
it's a purely, it's one of
the five federal academies

00:04:06.246 --> 00:04:11.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
of Air Force, Army, Navy,
Coast Guard, anyway.

00:04:12.418 --> 00:04:13.386
This is the book
they had me read.

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:16.422
So while my peers are going

00:04:16.422 --> 00:04:18.291
through traditional Snowflake U,

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:22.762 align:start size:97% position:3%
are studying Keynes and
Adam Smith and (indistinct),

00:04:23.963 --> 00:04:26.165
my economics teacher at
the academy had us read,

00:04:26.165 --> 00:04:30.970 align:start size:81% position:19%
Marx, Hitler, Mao,
Stalin, Lennon.

00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:34.140
So at 18 years old, Dave,
I'm effed up, you know,

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:37.076
I'm going "Holy Mackerel."

00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:40.013
And that's when the
kinda lights go on,

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:42.282
I'm 18 years old,
military school,

00:04:42.282 --> 00:04:44.617
I'm being yelled at screamed at.

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:47.453
And I realized that most of
my friends are communists,

00:04:48.321 --> 00:04:49.489
but they don't know it.

00:04:49.489 --> 00:04:51.024 align:start size:84% position:16%
I'm not saying
they're bad people,

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:55.228
just like, can you be a Hindu,

00:04:55.228 --> 00:04:57.330
can you be Christian,
can you be Muslim,

00:04:57.330 --> 00:04:58.264
can be Jewish?

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:01.834 align:start size:84% position:16%
Economics is
basically a religion.

00:05:01.834 --> 00:05:03.636
That's all it is.

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:08.107 align:start size:97% position:3%
So the moment my economics
teacher at the military school

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:10.343
is teaching me this
stuff, I'm going,

00:05:10.343 --> 00:05:12.578 align:start size:84% position:16%
"Most school teachers
are Marxists."

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:17.617
And that's kind of when
the lights kept going on.

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:20.086
So I graduated 1969.

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:21.587
My background is oil,

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:24.590
so I do know what I'm talking
about when it comes to oil.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:28.094
So when that sucker Biden cut
off the Keystone XL Pipeline,

00:05:28.094 --> 00:05:29.996
I said, "That man's a communist

00:05:29.996 --> 00:05:31.631 align:start size:84% position:16%
"'cause I know
what he was up to."

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:34.300
I mean, I'm an oil guy,
I sell for Standard Oil.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:36.602
My first port of call
was Valdez Alaska,

00:05:36.602 --> 00:05:41.474
the Alaska Pipeline in 1969,
I'm going "Holy Mackerel."

00:05:41.474 --> 00:05:44.911
Then I could see communism
seeping into our country,

00:05:44.911 --> 00:05:47.680
plus I'm so old,
Columbia University

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:52.685 align:start size:97% position:3%
was one of the first ones that
had the riots in the '60s,

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:55.154
and the riots then spread
through all the colleges

00:05:55.154 --> 00:05:56.789
throughout United States.

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:59.125 align:start size:84% position:16%
So that when you
read this book here,

00:05:59.125 --> 00:06:04.063
you'll find out that in 1930
communism came into America

00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:08.835 align:start size:97% position:3%
from the Frankfurt School
and they embedded themselves

00:06:08.835 --> 00:06:11.104 align:start size:88% position:13%
in Columbia University's
Teachers College.

00:06:12.238 --> 00:06:17.043 align:start size:88% position:13%
And so that was in 1930s
and as a baby boomer

00:06:18.244 --> 00:06:23.249 align:start size:81% position:19%
I go to Vietnam
twice '66 and '72,

00:06:24.117 --> 00:06:25.585
I fly for the U.S. Marine Corps

00:06:25.585 --> 00:06:28.154 align:start size:97% position:3%
not the Japanese Marine Corps,
but the U.S. Marine Corps.

00:06:28.154 --> 00:06:30.256
- Noted, I will
make note of that

00:06:31.657 --> 00:06:33.192 align:start size:97% position:3%
in the comment section.
- I'm fighting for freedom.

00:06:33.192 --> 00:06:34.794
I am fighting for freedom,

00:06:34.794 --> 00:06:37.497
and I'm watching the news, Dave,

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:42.535
what our press was reporting
wasn't what was happening.

00:06:42.535 --> 00:06:44.704
And the only reason I knew that,

00:06:44.704 --> 00:06:46.773
because I fought in the battles

00:06:46.773 --> 00:06:48.608 align:start size:84% position:16%
they were describing
on television.

00:06:49.575 --> 00:06:51.144
So this sounded like blaspheme,

00:06:51.144 --> 00:06:52.879 align:start size:84% position:16%
so when Walter
Cronkite, you know,

00:06:54.414 --> 00:06:55.882
the Grand Puba of journalism,

00:06:55.882 --> 00:06:58.351
"And that tonight is
the CBS Evening News."

00:06:58.351 --> 00:07:00.153
I said, "You're lying to us."

00:07:01.621 --> 00:07:05.391 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's, you know,
Dave, that's when I went,

00:07:05.391 --> 00:07:06.859
"We're being screwed."

00:07:06.859 --> 00:07:09.929
And I realized this book
is an 1848 was coming true,

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:11.798
it's only 50 pages.

00:07:11.798 --> 00:07:13.366
Most people have never read it.

00:07:15.435 --> 00:07:16.702
So that's why-
- All right,

00:07:16.702 --> 00:07:18.638
so you've given me a lot
of avenues to go there.

00:07:18.638 --> 00:07:22.074 align:start size:94% position:6%
So first, I love that
you started by connecting

00:07:22.074 --> 00:07:24.744
capitalism to freedom

00:07:24.744 --> 00:07:27.914
because we seem to be
losing both right now.

00:07:27.914 --> 00:07:30.650
So to connect this a
little bit directly

00:07:30.650 --> 00:07:35.655
to capitalism at the moment,
how do you think capitalism,

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:38.057 align:start size:88% position:13%
or why do you think,
perhaps, that capitalism

00:07:38.057 --> 00:07:41.093 align:start size:84% position:16%
didn't sell itself
well enough right now?

00:07:41.093 --> 00:07:44.163 align:start size:97% position:3%
Like the sales people for
capitalism maybe are failing,

00:07:44.163 --> 00:07:46.933
and that, seemingly, is
why the ideas of the book

00:07:46.933 --> 00:07:49.702 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you keep holding
up, "Communist Manifesto"

00:07:49.702 --> 00:07:53.706
for our audio listeners,
seems to be taking off.

00:07:53.706 --> 00:07:55.308
- Well, when I wrote
"Rich Dad, Poor Dad"

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:58.010 align:start size:88% position:13%
which came out in 1997,
it was turned down

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:00.646
by every one of those
Marxist book editors

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:01.581
in New York (laughs).

00:08:01.581 --> 00:08:03.416
- Unbelievable. Unbelievable.

00:08:03.416 --> 00:08:04.517 align:start size:81% position:19%
- You know what
I'm talking about.

00:08:04.517 --> 00:08:05.785
- They're all crumbling now,

00:08:05.785 --> 00:08:08.554
so you're getting
your just rewards.

00:08:08.554 --> 00:08:12.325 align:start size:97% position:3%
- And I asked them, I
asked the question in 1997,

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.461
I published the book,

00:08:15.461 --> 00:08:17.230
"So what does school
teach you about money?"

00:08:19.098 --> 00:08:19.932
Why not?

00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:24.770
And then that's when those
Marxists in New York City

00:08:24.770 --> 00:08:26.239
couldn't answer the
question and said,

00:08:26.239 --> 00:08:28.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, you don't know what
you're talking about."

00:08:28.641 --> 00:08:30.142
And I said, "What do you mean?"

00:08:30.142 --> 00:08:33.179 align:start size:97% position:3%
He says, "Well, you talk about
the rich not paying taxes."

00:08:33.179 --> 00:08:35.147
I said, "That's correct."

00:08:35.147 --> 00:08:38.684
So if you understand taxes,

00:08:38.684 --> 00:08:42.722 align:start size:84% position:16%
taxes came in in 1913
with the creation

00:08:42.722 --> 00:08:47.727
of the Federal Reserve Bank,
the Fed is a central bank.

00:08:49.161 --> 00:08:51.531
Doesn't that send chills
up and down your spine?

00:08:51.531 --> 00:08:52.598
So in 1913-

00:08:52.598 --> 00:08:54.534
- It does now. It does now.

00:08:54.534 --> 00:08:55.935
Maybe it didn't 10 years ago,

00:08:55.935 --> 00:08:57.870 align:start size:88% position:13%
but I was very
different 10 years ago.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.772
- And, Dave, 10 years ago,

00:08:59.772 --> 00:09:02.375 align:start size:88% position:13%
if you and I were having
this conversation,

00:09:02.375 --> 00:09:04.977
the little white men in
the little rubber suit

00:09:04.977 --> 00:09:06.479
would be dragging
me out the door.

00:09:06.479 --> 00:09:09.549
(both laughing)

00:09:09.549 --> 00:09:11.918
So I said, you know, I mean,

00:09:11.918 --> 00:09:13.452 align:start size:84% position:16%
"What did they teach
you about money?"

00:09:13.452 --> 00:09:15.788
And they go, "Nothing."

00:09:15.788 --> 00:09:18.324 align:start size:84% position:16%
I said, "Ever asked
yourself why?"

00:09:18.324 --> 00:09:19.959
"Well, no, 'cause money is,

00:09:19.959 --> 00:09:21.827
"the love of money is
the root of all evil."

00:09:21.827 --> 00:09:23.095
Some of that Christian stuff.

00:09:23.095 --> 00:09:25.464
I'm going, "I'm not
knocking Christians,

00:09:25.464 --> 00:09:26.732
"I'm just saying, you know,

00:09:26.732 --> 00:09:28.901
"it's a lot of religious
indoctrination in money.

00:09:30.169 --> 00:09:31.370
"If you study money,

00:09:31.370 --> 00:09:33.105 align:start size:84% position:16%
"that means you're
gonna be greedy, evil,

00:09:33.105 --> 00:09:35.608 align:start size:88% position:13%
"and be a sex trafficker
or something."

00:09:35.608 --> 00:09:38.377
I'm going, "Man, there's
so much stuff attached

00:09:38.377 --> 00:09:40.279 align:start size:84% position:16%
"to this little
subject called money."

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:43.449
So capitalism to me
is just basically

00:09:43.449 --> 00:09:45.484 align:start size:88% position:13%
free market capitalism,
it's freedom.

00:09:45.484 --> 00:09:48.421 align:start size:94% position:6%
You wanna be a communist,
knock yourself out.

00:09:48.421 --> 00:09:51.724 align:start position:0%
And most teachers are communist,
they just don't know it.

00:09:51.724 --> 00:09:54.493 align:start size:84% position:16%
They don't understand
that taxes,

00:09:54.493 --> 00:09:57.697
what Marx said about a
progressive income tax

00:09:57.697 --> 00:09:59.899
is essential for the
spread of communism.

00:10:01.133 --> 00:10:03.769
You know, it's right
in the book, read it.

00:10:03.769 --> 00:10:05.972
- Do you think that they don't,

00:10:05.972 --> 00:10:07.206 align:start size:84% position:16%
it's interesting
because you're saying

00:10:07.206 --> 00:10:08.407
they don't know that
they're communist,

00:10:08.407 --> 00:10:09.942
but do you think they
also fundamentally

00:10:09.942 --> 00:10:13.379 align:start size:88% position:13%
don't seem to understand
a certain part of
human psychology,

00:10:13.379 --> 00:10:14.680
the way we actually work?

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.449
What actually drives us,

00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:18.484 align:start size:88% position:13%
the way we wanna
maintain relationships,

00:10:18.484 --> 00:10:20.720 align:start size:84% position:16%
that there are
win-wins in business,

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:21.821
things of that nature?

00:10:23.055 --> 00:10:24.757
- Well, I'll tell
you what in my,

00:10:24.757 --> 00:10:26.225
and I didn't do well in school.

00:10:26.225 --> 00:10:29.662
I mean, I went, only reason
